<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29559" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστῠχ-έω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδυστύχεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.105
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδυστύχησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Mx.</u>
					243a
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδυστύχηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>La.</u>
					183c
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.55
			</span></i>, Lyc.Trag.<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, v. infr.:—<i>to be unlucky,
				unfortunate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεύχομαι τῷδε μὲν εὐτυχεῖν . .
					τοῖσι δὲ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					482
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1159
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					424
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παίδων πέρι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					713
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1449
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>La.</u>
					183c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ γῆν καὶ κατὰ θάλατταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					2.148d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cam.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα δυστυχῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					429
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστυχεῖν ἄμορφον γυναῖκα</span>”
				<i>to be curst with . . ,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					11.287
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μανίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ach.Tat.
					4.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἀλλοδαπῆς βαρυτέραν τὴν πατρίδα
					δυστυχήσασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.16
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			 in same sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν τις
				δυστυχηθῇ</span>
			<i>is made unfortunate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				877e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὑφ᾽ ἑτέρων δυστυχηθέντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.70
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
